<<<
Some sentences picked out from the Enc. Brit. article on molecule may throw light; but here, first, are the etymological meanings: molecule, small mass; atom, uncuttable (particle); electron, amber; corpuscle, small body.
===
Some sentences picked out from the *Enc. Brit.* article on *molecule* may throw light; but here, first, are the etymological meanings: *molecule*, small mass; *atom*, uncuttable (particle); *electron*, amber; *corpuscle*, small body.
>>>

